# 15. Development Philosophy

The project MUST NOT be built as one huge code dump.

Development will happen incrementally.

The AI developer must:

1. Understand the complete project context first.
2. Implement only the assigned phase.
3. Run/test the implementation.
4. Report problems.
5. Fix issues.
6. Verify that the phase works.
7. Only then proceed to the next phase.

Do NOT implement future modules prematurely.

Do NOT randomly change the agreed architecture.

Do NOT remove an existing working feature just to implement a new feature.

Do NOT rewrite the entire project unless there is a genuine technical reason.

