# 17. Critical Development Rule

The mandatory disease-detection model is the highest priority.

Optional features must NEVER compromise:

* Disease model performance
* Dataset integrity
* Evaluation correctness
* Reproducibility
* Project stability

The official evaluation gives significant importance to the held-out core macro-F1 and reproducibility. Bonus modules are valuable only when they are actually functional and correctly implemented.

Therefore:

**Core quality > feature quantity.**

