# 20. Originality & AI-Assisted Development

Open-source libraries, pretrained models/backbones, and public datasets may be used where permitted, but their sources must be properly cited.

Do not copy an entire public project/notebook.

AI coding assistants may be used, but the resulting system must be genuinely developed, understood, tested, and reproducible.

The repository should contain an appropriate originality declaration and third-party references where required.

